{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++17 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++17 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nconst int MOD = 1000000007;\nusing i64 = long long;\n\nint power_mod(int x, int y) {\n    int res = 1;\n    while (y) {\n        if (y & 1) res = (i64)res * x % MOD;\n        x = (i64)x * x % MOD;\n        y >>= 1;\n    }\n    return res;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios_base::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(0);\n\n    int n;\n    cin >> n;\n\n    vector<vector<int>> p(n, vector<int>(n));\n    int inv100 = power_mod(100, MOD - 2);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            cin >> p[i][j];\n            p[i][j] = (i64)p[i][j] * inv100 % MOD;\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Precompute subsets of each size and their IDs\n    vector<vector<int>> comb(n + 1);\n    vector<vector<int>> sid(n + 1, vector<int>(1 << n, -1));\n    for (int sz = 0; sz <= n; ++sz) {\n        for (int mask = 0; mask < (1 << n); ++mask) {\n            if (__builtin_popcount(mask) == sz) {\n                sid[sz][mask] = (int)comb[sz].size();\n                comb[sz].push_back(mask);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    vector<map<i64, int>> dp(n + 1);\n    dp[0][1] = 1;\n\n    for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {\n        for (int s = 0; s < (1 << n); ++s) {\n            int prob = 1;\n            for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n                if ((s >> j) & 1) {\n                    prob = (i64)prob * p[i - 1][j] % MOD;\n                } else {\n                    prob = (i64)prob * ((1 - p[i - 1][j] + MOD) % MOD) % MOD;\n                }\n            }\n\n            for (const auto &pr : dp[i - 1]) {\n                i64 mask_old = pr.first;\n                int val_old = pr.second;\n                i64 mask_new = 0;\n\n                for (int t : comb[i]) {\n                    // Test if t is \"compatible\" with s and old mask\n                    bool ok = false;\n                    int ttemp = t;\n                    while (ttemp) {\n                        int bit = ttemp & -ttemp;\n                        int j = __builtin_ctz(bit);\n                        if ((s & bit) && (mask_old & (1LL << sid[i - 1][t ^ bit]))) {\n                            ok = true;\n                            break;\n                        }\n                        ttemp ^= bit;\n                    }\n                    if (ok) {\n                        mask_new |= (1LL << sid[i][t]);\n                    }\n                }\n\n                dp[i][mask_new] = (dp[i][mask_new] + (i64)val_old * prob) % MOD;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    cout << dp[n][1] << \"\\n\";\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\nMOD = 1000000007\n\ndef power_mod(x, y):\n    res = 1\n    while y:\n        if y & 1:\n            res = (res * x) % MOD\n        x = (x * x) % MOD\n        y >>= 1\n    return res\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    it = iter(data)\n    n = int(next(it))\n    p = [[0]*n for _ in range(n)]\n    inv100 = power_mod(100, MOD-2)\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(n):\n            val = int(next(it))\n            p[i][j] = (val * inv100) % MOD\n\n    # Precompute subsets of each size and their IDs\n    comb = [[] for _ in range(n+1)]\n    sid = [{} for _ in range(n+1)]  # sid[sz] maps mask -> index\n    for sz in range(n+1):\n        for mask in range(1 << n):\n            if mask.bit_count() == sz:\n                sid[sz][mask] = len(comb[sz])\n                comb[sz].append(mask)\n\n    dp = [{} for _ in range(n+1)]\n    dp[0][1] = 1  # mask=1 corresponds to the empty subset (size 0)\n\n    for i in range(1, n+1):\n        for s in range(1 << n):\n            prob = 1\n            for j in range(n):\n                if (s >> j) & 1:\n                    prob = (prob * p[i-1][j]) % MOD\n                else:\n                    prob = (prob * ((1 - p[i-1][j] + MOD) % MOD)) % MOD\n\n            for mask_old, val_old in dp[i-1].items():\n                mask_new = 0\n                for t in comb[i]:\n                    # check compatibility\n                    ok = False\n                    ttemp = t\n                    while ttemp:\n                        bit = ttemp & -ttemp\n                        j = (bit.bit_length() - 1)\n                        if (s & bit) and (mask_old & (1 << sid[i-1][t ^ bit])):\n                            ok = True\n                            break\n                        ttemp ^= bit\n                    if ok:\n                        mask_new |= (1 << sid[i][t])\n                dp[i][mask_new] = (dp[i].get(mask_new, 0) + val_old * prob) % MOD\n\n    print(dp[n][1] % MOD)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-2.407998726994265e-05, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.00039402826223522425, -0.004249471705406904, 0.0, -0.20141839981079102, -0.00043096792069263756, -2.264974000354414e-06, -4.768370445162